--- COMPANION (two-sided): winner-index speckle (MEASURED) ---
index speckle   : 0.003% of pixels differ by more than 2 from their 3x3 median index
                  On the REGULARISED winner, the same statistic and tolerance `strehl stack`
                  reports for argmax. Unlike mean|grad| this is two-sided: a real scene gives
                  smooth depth with sharp edges, and BOTH over-smoothing and manufactured
                  detail move it away from that.
                  Fact 23's 34.4% -> 0.868% pair is BOTH the retired ring operator, unregularised
                  then 17x17-regularised (M2-verification section 4; :205 states the measure
                  was the ring difference, and Tenengrad did not exist until M14). NEITHER is a
                  Tenengrad number, and no section-4 row publishes a regularised-Tenengrad
                  speckle at all, so there is no cross-operator reference to quote here. The
                  operator-matched figure is fact 71's 1.010% for UNREGULARISED Tenengrad on
                  this ROI; the regularised comparable is this run's own value, above.
